# ─── Prettier does NOT own the source in this repository ────────────────────
#
# This is the decision the file exists to record, because the obvious setup is
# the other way round and somebody will try it.
#
# MEASURED, not assumed. Run across the 172 hand-written .ts/.tsx/.mjs files at
# printWidth 100 — the p90 line here is 80 characters and the p99 is 102, so the
# width is not the disagreement — Prettier rewrites 157 of them: +10,396 / −5,066
# lines against 33,402 total. It grows the codebase by a sixth and touches
# roughly a third of its lines.
#
# The churn is not cosmetic. It explodes deliberately-grouped JSX props one per
# line, so
#
#     variant="ghost" size="icon" aria-label={label} title={label}
#
# — one thought, one line — becomes four. It does the same to destructured
# parameter lists and to `cn(...)` calls whose arguments are grouped by what they
# style. This codebase's formatting carries meaning that a general-purpose
# printer cannot see, and trading that for "nobody argues about commas" is a bad
# trade when nobody is arguing about commas.
#
# So Prettier is left with what has no house style to lose — JSON, YAML and CSS —
# and the source is formatted by the people writing it. ESLint covers what
# actually breaks (eslint.config.mjs).
#
# TO REVERSE THIS, delete the lines in either block below and run `pnpm format`.
# It is one commit and a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` entry. Deliberately easy to
# undo, and deliberately not the default.
*.ts
*.tsx
*.mts
*.mjs

# ─── Nor the documents ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Same finding, measured the same way. `docs/DESIGN.md` alone differs by 697
# lines. Two reasons, and neither is configurable away:
#
#   Tables are padded to column width. Every future edit to one cell re-pads the
#   whole table, so a one-word change arrives as a fifteen-line diff — in the
#   files where the diff IS the review.
#
#   `*emphasis*` becomes `_emphasis_`, everywhere, in every document.
#
# These documents are the primary artifact of this project. `proseWrap:
# "preserve"` in .prettierrc.json keeps the paragraphs intact for the day this
# is reconsidered; the rest is not worth the churn.
*.md

# ─── Nor the one HTML file ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `index.html` is a shell around a thirty-line comment explaining the renderer's
# CSP line by line. Prettier indents the `<!--` and leaves the body where it was,
# so the explanation ends up misaligned against its own opening. One file, one
# hand-formatted essay, nothing to gain.
*.html

