# Tool-managed. These are rewritten by the tools that own them, so formatting one
# is undone the next time it runs — and `format:check` then fails over a file
# nobody edited. Caught exactly that way: graphify rewrote .codex/hooks.json
# between a `format` and a `format:check`.
.codex/
# Same, from the icon pipeline. The file is gitignored, but Prettier does not
# read .gitignore — and it is written with JSON.stringify(…, 2), which puts every
# array element on its own line while Prettier collapses the short ones back.
# Neither yields to the other, so `format:check` fails over a file nobody edited.
packages/icons/incomplete-icons.json

